ms, and events"}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2021-02-28T08:52:12Z","updated_at":"2021-03-03T23:52:30Z","closed_at":"2021-03-03T23:52:30Z","author_association":"MEMBER","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bevy version\r\n\r\nbc4fe9b (latest main)\r\n\r\n## Operating system & version\r\n\r\nArch linux\r\n\r\n## What you did\r\n\r\nI accidentally registered a system with a signature including `&mut Commands` and a Query using `.exclusive_system()`\r\n\r\n## What you expected to happen\r\n\r\nCompile failure, or maybe for it to just work normally.\r\n\r\n## What actually happened\r\n\r\nThe program compiled and the system ran apparently as normal. The query returned results but commands scheduled with Commands never got applied.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nIn this example you can see that a component is removed using Commands which should cause the Query to stop returning results after the first frame but instead the same entity is returned every frame:\r\n\r\n```rust\r\n use bevy::prelude::*;\r\n\r\n fn main() {\r\n     App::build()\r\n         .add_plugins(DefaultPlugins)\r\n         .add_startup_system(setup.system())\r\n         .add_system(removal.exclusive_system())\r\n         .run();\r\n }\r\n\r\n struct MyMarkerA;\r\n struct MyMarkerB;\r\n\r\n fn setup(\r\n     commands: &mut Commands,\r\n ) {\r\n     commands.spawn((MyMarkerA, MyMarkerB));\r\n }\r\n\r\n fn removal(\r\n     commands: &mut Commands,\r\n     query: Query<(Entity, &MyMarkerA, &MyMarkerB)>,\r\n ) {\r\n!    for (entity, a, b) in query.iter() {\r\n         println!(\"{:?}\", entity);\r\n         commands.remove_one::<MyMarkerA>(entity);\r\n     }\r\n }\r\n ```","closed_by":{"login":"bors[bot]","id":26634292,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90MjY2Mz